b8f5525d (3189 1792919604790 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f330-f336") (src . "search answers over the dispatcher's state; context gains --working\n\nThe search verb ignored the state the dispatcher hands every verb and\nopened and reduced the store on each call, so a resident daemon folded\nthe whole store again per search (about as long as its own start-up\nload). It now takes its view through reduction-for as every read verb\ndoes; store.sc gains search-state-report beside store-search-report,\nboth under one limit rule. Same state, same report: the answer bytes do\nnot depend on which was asked. As a connection-local read, search now\nanswers the publication as it stands, as read does.\n\ncontext gains --working: the material is assembled over the request\nwriter's working view, the committed state at the drafts' cut with that\nwriter's drafts laid over it, in a fresh query session, never the kept\none. The answer carries (working \"<writer>\") after `for`, counted in the\nbudget; a refusal of the view (writer-required, invalid-working-writer,\nworking-unavailable, working-draft-unreadable) is the answer; an id the\nview does not hold is answered as read answers it over that view. Drafts\nare not change events, so validity and the other hard queries answer the\ncommitted rows; the premises of drafted blocks are the overlay's and are\nnot handed to a commit.\n\nThe reduction record gains an overlay mark, set only on a working view.\nThe process-wide caches kept by applied cut for committed states (the\ndefinitions index, the file-header and children tables) never answer for\nan overlay, which shares the committed cut: an overlay's index and tables\nlive in their own slots, keyed by the state's identity and the catalogue\ngeneration.\n\n- rpc.sc: search over (reduction-for store state) through\n  search-state-report; dispatch-helper hands out working-state.\n- store.sc: search-state-report, check-search-limit; the overlay slots\n  beside the committed caches.\n- context.sc, extensions.sc: the flag, the view, the marker inside the\n  reserved and rendered form, the usage and option table.\n- reduce.sc: the overlay field, copied by reduce-clone.\n- working.sc: overlay-drafts marks the view it builds.\n- README: the context section.\n- Tests: daemon-session A-6..A-8 and SESS-W; cli3 N9; context-verb\n  CW-0..CW-12; read-receipt C48a-1 (search answers at the given state);\n  unreadable-acknowledge-routes D-interleave (search is no longer held);\n  rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 472))))
